WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.415 --> 00:00:05.500
My name's Donna Cropley.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.208
I'll give you a little
bit of background,

00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:10.570
I'm a senior admin assistant
over at Yale School

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.710
of Public Health.

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:14.680
And I work in the Environmental
Health Sciences department.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.280
And my chair this year
is going to teach,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.860
or has taught, public health
toxicology, which is EHS 503.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:30.190
And I was given the task
to create everything

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.650
for the students in Canvas.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:37.160
So I had Jenn come
over to EPH with us

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.370
and sit down with the
chair because he is new

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:43.420
to the school, new to teaching,
and this is new to Canvas.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:46.210
So I had to have a meeting to
have everybody there to see

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.955
what does he want to use Canvas
for and how can we get there.

00:00:49.955 --> 00:00:52.330
So we did have a couple of
meetings, actually, with Jenn.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.610
And we had some snafus
in the beginning.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.680
But thanks to Canvas,
we worked it out.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.995
So I have further
copies of the syllabus

00:01:00.995 --> 00:01:03.370
up here, if you'd like to see
it, because as you can see,

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:06.530
it only goes to, I
believe, April 7th.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.740
And then the final is this week.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.040
So when I first
took a look at this,

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.590
and then knew what Canvas
has, my thought was to--

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:21.310
he's having lectures on
Monday, discussions on Friday,

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.700
so I thought, well, why
don't we create modules?

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.360
That was my thinking.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.590
So as soon as the syllabus
was done and finalized,

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:35.640
I went into Canvas, and
I created everything

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.210
you see here in the modules.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:45.790
So I did lecture first,
with the date, title.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.100
And on the syllabus,
he didn't put

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:52.460
in there lecture one,
discussion two, like that.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.330
So for the students,
I went in and I

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:59.010
did lecture one, the title, and
who the speaker is going to be.

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:01.570
It's himself, and he has
guest speakers come in.

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:04.487
So that's the way I
created it in Canvas.

00:02:04.487 --> 00:02:06.070
And the only way
that you can see that

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.028
is if I show it to you.

00:02:07.028 --> 00:02:09.580
[LAUGHTER]

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:13.920
So Let me just get out of here.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:14.910
Is it ending?

00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:18.375
Nope.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.325
There we go.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:36.700
[INAUDIBLE]

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.870
OK, and here's the modules.

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.020
And as you can see-- because
when there was a presentation,

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.512
I would be the one uploading
it to the students,

00:02:43.512 --> 00:02:45.220
hopefully, a few days
before the lecture.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.420
That's what he prefers.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:49.120
Sometimes it's the morning of.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.660
So I went in and, as you
can see, everything here,

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:57.050
I created, lecture one, and
then the discussion after it.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:00.370
And they would know that
lecture one is the first one.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.750
And what I chose to do--

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.480
he kind of left it up to me--

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.780
but what I chose to
do is not publish

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:09.460
until something was in there.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.990
That's what I chose to do.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.850
And a couple of pointers,
if anyone in here

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.410
is going to do that.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.280
We found out uploading
PowerPoint wasn't so great.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.860
So you have to
take the PowerPoint

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.900
and convert it to PDF.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.067
And the students were
able to get that better.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:26.650
So we found that out
on the beginning.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.250
[CHUCKLES] So we did
that, so everything's PDF.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:36.870
And the other thing,
I would publish,

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:40.550
but I also, on top of that,
have to send announcements

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:41.730
to the students.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.880
I guess they don't always
see, oh, something's there.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.270
So now, every time I publish,
I go into Announcement

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.850
and I just send an announcement.

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:54.220
We learned this throughout.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:57.850
And as you can see, these are
all my announcements to them.

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.920
Every time I
published something,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.306
I would let them
know, hey, it's here.

00:04:02.306 --> 00:04:03.680
So they know when
it's available,

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.240
whether it's two days
before, maybe the morning of.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.000
So that's what I
utilized Canvas for.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.460
And that's the way, when
I first looked at it,

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:18.160
that I saw how to do it, in my
mind, was to put it in modules.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.990
Obviously, before I
uploaded the syllabus

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:22.510
to syllabus, which
you can see in here--

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.940
I don't know how many
people have utilized

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.347
any of these this
disks-- but of course,

00:04:27.347 --> 00:04:28.930
the syllabus is
there, as you can see.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.990
Really, that's about it.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.760
But those are my two pointers.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.186
And then, we go down.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.350
Here, there's an option in
there to have the discussions

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:49.120
indented a little bit.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.380
So sometimes, the presenters
would have their presentation

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:55.480
and also papers, maybe.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:58.270
So I just make it in a
way where you look at it,

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:01.870
you understand it, kind of
like looking at the syllabus

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.090
was, in my mind, how
I was looking at it.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:09.090
So that's what I utilized
Canvas for, so I don't know.

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.670
[LAUGHS] Just to give you
an idea what it looks like.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:14.650
And we'll be doing
this next spring, too.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:15.418
Yes?

00:05:15.418 --> 00:05:17.908
Is it true that, when
you send an announcement,

00:05:17.908 --> 00:05:19.402
it doesn't go to
the regular email?

00:05:19.402 --> 00:05:20.400
I heard that.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:20.940
Correct.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:22.990
My understanding is
it is through Canvas.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:25.290
So you have to go into
Canvas to [INAUDIBLE]?

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.727
I believe so,
because I know when--

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.310
although, when I
send an announcement,

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.190
I do get an email that I did it.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.070
Yes.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.590
So I'll just speak to that.

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:36.296
It does get sent out to
your Yale email account,

00:05:36.296 --> 00:05:38.730
but every person can
control what notifications

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:39.720
they receive.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.400
So if they feel like
somebody's posting

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.340
way too many announcements,
they can turn off Announcements

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.110
so that they won't
keep getting those.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:49.080
But the default setting is
that they would receive emails

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.790
whenever an
announcement is posted.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:55.470
And I think that was the problem
is it's left up to the students

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:58.150
to have that Announcement
piece on or off.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:03.110
So some would say to the
faculty member, I never got it.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.160
And I'm like, my god, I sent it.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.325
And then, we were finding out
who has it on, who has it off.

00:06:08.325 --> 00:06:09.600
You don't know.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.810
So the best thing is to
just do an announcement.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.280
And they're supposed
to all get it.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.170
So I hope they do.

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:21.805
And it worked, after we
worked that out a little bit.

00:06:21.805 --> 00:06:24.576
So I don't know if there's any--

00:06:24.576 --> 00:06:26.000
You mentioned that
you were having

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.760
a problem with the PowerPoints.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.400
Is that because the PowerPoints
were a lower file size?

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:33.450
Or did you have special
transitions in PowerPoint

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.620
that just didn't carry over?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.880
Probably both.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.310
I'm thinking the files
were probably pretty big.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:45.010
The lecture's an
hour and a half.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:49.022
And I've seen 75 slides.

00:06:49.022 --> 00:06:50.980
You might have figures
in there and everything,

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.450
so think that was the problem.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.300
I really never found out,
but the easy, quick fix

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.890
is just to do PDF.

00:06:56.890 --> 00:07:00.440
And they were able to
download it that way.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.794
It was much better.

00:07:02.794 --> 00:07:04.040
So that's-- sure.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.540
Did you get any feedback
from the students

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.040
about being able to
navigate this way,

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:13.040
rather than ways you might
have done it in the past?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:16.910
In Classes*v2, it was
a different instructor.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.880
And he didn't utilize it the
way that this professor does.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.670
He just would put
slides up there.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.800
And he didn't have
guest lecturers.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.390
You know, this is
very detailed, which

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.220
is the way he was running it.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:31.160
Classes*v2 was very easy--
a few slides here and there,

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.740
so it was more easier.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:39.200
With Canvas-- I did hear
we have a TA for the class.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.710
And they would like
everything through Canvas.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:43.757
They like Canvas.

00:07:43.757 --> 00:07:46.340
They like the Assignment piece,
or the Paper piece, everything

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.110
to be through Canvas.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:51.020
So we decided to go that
way, rather than email.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:53.780
Don't email me the final,
or wherever they're using,

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:56.300
the TA is taking
care of that piece.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:08:00.980
And they said that to her, and
then she came back and told us.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:05.150
And this is PDFs of what
the PowerPoint would be,

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:08.890
not what the resources are?

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:14.820
Or do people use the modules
for resources as well?

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.940
And you wouldn't put
them in the other place,

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:18.720
you'd put them in this place?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.230
Resources?

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:21.090
You mean papers?

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:23.050
PDFs that you'd file-- files.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:23.550
Yeah.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:26.690
I Use it in modules, because
they would give papers, which

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.080
were PDFs, as part of the--

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.459
like, say it's a discussion,
and it's two papers

00:08:31.459 --> 00:08:32.500
they're going to discuss.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.360
So it's a PDF.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.432
So I put it in that
piece that's Discussion--

00:08:35.432 --> 00:08:37.890
you can see it in there-- and
I would upload the two papers

00:08:37.890 --> 00:08:42.390
and explain the two
files attached are part

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:46.850
of the discussion today, which
is really a lot of information,

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.410
so specifically, they
know what's going on.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:52.740
And like I said, they
seemed to like that piece.

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:53.865
There was a question there.

00:08:58.755 --> 00:09:02.667
I think that the benefit to the
students in putting everything

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:05.112
they need for that
session, the readings,

00:09:05.112 --> 00:09:09.530
the links to the discussions, if
they're submitting assignments,

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:14.290
PowerPoints, in Classes*v2, they
would need to go to one place

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:19.154
to find the files, another
place to find the discussion.

00:09:19.154 --> 00:09:21.539
This way, all they need
to do is go to modules,

00:09:21.539 --> 00:09:22.500
and then we're not
going to miss anything.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:23.000
Right.

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:28.090
And my thought was, this one
week, this week is a module.

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:30.700
He had a lecture on Monday,
what's attached to that?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.950
Underneath, because it's
Friday, is a discussion.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.120
What's attached there?

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.079
So they can look at it.

00:09:35.079 --> 00:09:37.286
And I think, pretty much,
I put dates on all of them.

00:09:37.286 --> 00:09:38.740
For me, I had to
have the dates--

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.156
you know, what's going on April
3rd, what's going on April

00:09:41.156 --> 00:09:44.670
10th, basically, what this is.

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:47.170
So that's the way
I looked at it.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:48.250
I think it works.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.875
So I'm going to do the same next
year, unless I hear different.

00:09:50.875 --> 00:09:51.498
[LAUGHTER]

00:09:51.498 --> 00:09:53.630
If you're teaching courses
where maybe there's

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.046
some overlap of
content, would you

00:09:55.046 --> 00:09:58.860
be able to just copy the
entire module from this course

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.750
and move it over
to another course?

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:01.710
I don't know.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:02.470
Absolutely.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:02.970
Yeah.

00:10:02.970 --> 00:10:05.310
You can definitely copy
content from any course.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:08.650
You can copy as much or as
little from another course.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.460
So you could do a
full course copy,

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.290
or you could be very
targeted and say,

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:14.790
I just want this
specific module,

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:18.650
or this specific file
from the files there.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:19.150
Great.

00:10:22.636 --> 00:10:24.130
I think I'm done, right?

00:10:27.116 --> 00:10:27.616
[APPLAUSE]

00:10:27.616 --> 00:10:31.102
Oh, thank you.

